    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 73.88 projection against Junis. His value is buoyed by a prime #2 hole placement and a favorable right-handed matchup, though we have slightly tempered his ceiling due to the drag of game-cap preservation relative to his 62% stolen base hold rate. Joining him in the \"Strong\" start tier is **Josh Naylor**, who draws a favorable spot against Lambert. **Josh Naylor**\u2019s move to the three-hole provides a significant 6% boost to his efficiency, cementing him as the primary anchor for our run production today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Dalton Rushing**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.43. While his elite pop-time profile is valuable, the optimizer prioritized benching him due to the stiff matchup against the 2.60 xERA of Trevor McDonald. Similarly, **Travis Bazzana** fell just short of our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" at 38.06, largely due to a difficult L/L platoon disadvantage against Suter. With **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young** currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status, we are leaning on projected spots, but these positions remain high-risk; should either be bumped from the lineup, we will be forced to reconsider our defensive depth behind the plate and at middle infield. **Cole Young** in particular is hovering near the floor at 40.36, and his performance against Lambert will be a key indicator of whether we need to rotate in more aggressive options like **Brice Turang** or **Carson Williams** for future sets.",
